 "template": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new Quotation. Set the Customer field to '{{v1}}' — IMPORTANT: the Customer field is an autocomplete dropdown, so you must type the name and then actually pick the matching option from the dropdown that appears, not just type the text; verify the customer name is filled in as a selected value on the form. Then add ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (use the product dropdown in the Order Lines tab and actually select an option from the dropdown), and set its Quantity to 3. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that product on the line, and (c) the untaxed amount (Amount Untaxed / 'Untaxed Amount') the app computes and displays on the quotation. Note: Odoo long-polls so the page is never network-idle — wait for concrete page elements instead.",
